# Endings: checked in this order on arrival day; the last one has no conditions.

card end_contact
type ending
when flag signal_contact
when res food >= 1
text Old Friend. The fleet makes Mars orbit carrying a dead orbiter's last telemetry and a crew who won't stop talking about it. Somewhere below, a small machine knows someone came back.

card end_followed
type ending
when flag echo_heard
text Company. Seven ships make orbit. Just above them, on a slightly higher path, the carrier is still transmitting every 11 seconds. Nobody has answered it yet.

card end_patience
type ending
when flag arrive_wait
text Patience. The fleet parks in a long orbit and watches a dust storm the size of a continent swallow the landing zone. When it clears, seven ships are still waiting above it, with margins thin as foil and every one of them intact.

card end_through
type ending
when flag arrive_hold
text Through the Dust. The fleet holds the plan. The storm reaches the landing zone hours after the last ship is down, and the last thing the cameras see from orbit is seven ships under an orange sky, hatches sealed.

card end_long_way
type ending
text The Long Way Round. Seven ships, one planet, and a log that's mostly propellant figures and small kindnesses. Mission Control sends one word: "Nominal." Everyone aboard knows it was more than that.
